# 4. Combat Vision

Combat is one of the most important features of SAOMMO.

The player should be able to physically control weapons rather than selecting attacks from a menu.

A sword attack should depend on factors such as:

* sword position
* sword movement
* sword velocity
* sword rotation
* attack direction
* collision with the target
* potentially attack angle and impact strength

The first implementation will use a simple and reliable collision system.

More advanced blade tracing and combat calculations can be added later.

---

# 5. World Vision

SAOMMO is intended to grow into a large persistent online world.

The final world may contain:

* cities
* villages
* fields
* forests
* mountains
* dungeons
* bosses
* NPCs
* quests
* shops
* players
* guilds
* equipment
* progression systems
* large-scale events

The initial development world will be intentionally small.

The project will first prove its gameplay in a small test environment.

Large-scale world technology such as World Partition, PCG, advanced streaming, and multiplayer replication will be introduced when the project actually requires them.

---

# 6. Long-Term MMORPG Vision

The long-term goal is a persistent multiplayer world.

Players should eventually be able to:

* create characters
* explore the world
* fight enemies
* obtain equipment
* level up
* complete quests
* interact with NPCs
* trade
* form groups
* form guilds
* participate in multiplayer combat
* explore dungeons
* fight bosses
* interact with a persistent world

The architecture must therefore remain modular and scalable.

However, MMO functionality is not part of the first playable prototype.

---

# 7. Development Philosophy

SAOMMO will be developed incrementally.

The project follows this rule:

> Every major system must work in a playable test environment before the next major system becomes the primary development focus.

The initial progression is:

